# Paths that must never reach the published repository.
#
# One repo-relative path prefix per line; `#` comments ignored. Files under
# these prefixes are written for us alone (approval procedures, chain admin
# runbooks, open weaknesses), so the published branch must not track them.
# scripts/dev/publishability-test.sh fails while any tracked path matches,
# which is what catches one arriving on `release/**` with a merge from
# `main`: `git rm` it there (docs/operator/cutting-the-public-repo.md).
#
# A banner saying "internal" inside a file excludes nothing. Put the file
# under a prefix listed here instead.
docs/internal/
